1
00:00:28,800 --> 00:00:32,299
"My Rival and Me"

2
00:00:32,300 --> 00:00:34,300
(Episode 6)

3
00:00:34,399 --> 00:00:35,520
I'd be the top, though.

4
00:00:37,333 --> 00:00:39,853
No, how can I assume I've gone gay?

5
00:00:39,885 --> 00:00:40,965
Wei Yanzi, stay calm.

6
00:00:41,184 --> 00:00:43,784
I can't lose my cool at a time like this.

7
00:00:44,404 --> 00:00:46,325
Sorry to keep you waiting.

8
00:00:49,119 --> 00:00:50,119
Here.

9
00:00:50,560 --> 00:00:51,560
Have some fruit.

10
00:00:51,679 --> 00:00:52,679
Oh, thanks.

11
00:01:02,759 --> 00:01:05,799
So this is your cat?

12
00:01:07,560 --> 00:01:08,560
Wow.

13
00:01:08,920 --> 00:01:10,400
He's so cute!

14
00:01:10,480 --> 00:01:11,680
Mm. He's smart, too.

15
00:01:12,560 --> 00:01:13,159
William.

16
00:01:13,239 --> 00:01:14,239
Hey.

17
00:01:14,799 --> 00:01:15,799
Come to Daddy.

18
00:01:17,400 --> 00:01:18,400
Come here.

19
00:01:21,400 --> 00:01:24,120
What did you just call him?

20
00:01:24,840 --> 00:01:25,840
William.

21
00:01:29,000 --> 00:01:30,000
Oh.

22
00:01:30,359 --> 00:01:31,439
You've got the same name.

23
00:01:32,840 --> 00:01:35,280
So you've secretly been
my daddy all this time?

24
00:01:36,200 --> 00:01:36,920
Tell me the truth.

25
00:01:37,200 --> 00:01:39,000
Do you often scold him just to get at me?

26
00:01:40,439 --> 00:01:41,560
No.

27
00:01:42,280 --> 00:01:44,799
I named him when I brought him home.

28
00:01:45,280 --> 00:01:46,280
Oh, right.

29
00:01:46,879 --> 00:01:48,120
Back then,

30
00:01:48,200 --> 00:01:49,519
when you sprained your ankle,

31
00:01:49,959 --> 00:01:50,959
I thought I'd

32
00:01:51,519 --> 00:01:52,519
give him a cameo.

33
00:01:54,480 --> 00:01:55,799
That's why I said

34
00:01:57,159 --> 00:01:59,640
you wouldn't get what that video meant.

35
00:02:00,799 --> 00:02:01,959
You didn't know his name.

36
00:02:03,805 --> 00:02:05,883
Oh, Gu Yiliang.

37
00:02:05,907 --> 00:02:07,506
He knew exactly what he was doing.

38
00:02:07,507 --> 00:02:09,107
A riot of blossoms dazzles the eyes.

39
00:02:09,108 --> 00:02:11,026
One look at Yiliang and my knees give way.

40
00:02:11,027 --> 00:02:12,067
Buddha help me, Yiliang.

41
00:02:12,068 --> 00:02:13,907
Let me say this once and for all.

42
00:02:13,908 --> 00:02:15,907
I, Wei Yanzi, am straight as an arrow.

43
00:02:16,054 --> 00:02:18,453
Think you can bend me? Bring it on.

44
00:02:21,199 --> 00:02:22,039
Don't move.

45
00:02:22,159 --> 00:02:23,159
Hold that pose.

46
00:02:23,400 --> 00:02:23,960
William.

47
00:02:24,319 --> 00:02:25,319
Open your eyes wide.

48
00:02:34,560 --> 00:02:36,120
Hey, William! William!

49
00:02:36,400 --> 00:02:37,400
Let him go play.

50
00:02:40,400 --> 00:02:41,959
This is so cozy.

51
00:02:41,960 --> 00:02:44,839
Wei Yanzi, you've got someone now.

52
00:02:45,166 --> 00:02:46,519
Someone to lean on. [Someone to top]

53
00:02:46,520 --> 00:02:47,718
The “Yi” [Top] in Gu Yiliang.

54
00:02:47,719 --> 00:02:49,912
How come he gets to be the top?

55
00:02:49,936 --> 00:02:51,515
No way. Bring it on.

56
00:03:02,800 --> 00:03:05,759
My two Williams.

57
00:03:09,000 --> 00:03:11,240
I'm so done for.

58
00:03:17,680 --> 00:03:20,360
I'm going to the bathroom.

59
00:03:40,840 --> 00:03:41,840
Douya.

60
00:03:42,159 --> 00:03:43,159
What do I do?

61
00:03:44,199 --> 00:03:46,159
My rival just gave me

62
00:03:47,000 --> 00:03:48,960
a seriously horny look.

63
00:03:50,759 --> 00:03:52,120
Was that a hint?

64
00:03:55,400 --> 00:03:56,759
Are we really going to...

65
00:03:57,520 --> 00:03:58,080
do it?

66
00:03:58,280 --> 00:04:00,638
Your query violates public decency

67
00:04:00,639 --> 00:04:02,438
and carries significant risks.

68
00:04:02,439 --> 00:04:03,879
Please stop immediately.

69
00:04:05,159 --> 00:04:06,639
What good are you?

70
00:04:08,439 --> 00:04:09,439
Ugh.

71
00:04:09,919 --> 00:04:12,360
Maybe I shouldn't have
walked out like that.

72
00:04:13,879 --> 00:04:16,000
Does he think I can't handle it?

73
00:04:22,360 --> 00:04:25,360
I just didn't think we'd move this fast.

74
00:04:26,160 --> 00:04:28,199
I haven't even lined up any roles for him.

75
00:04:30,480 --> 00:04:31,480
Gu Yiliang.

76
00:04:31,600 --> 00:04:31,959
Yeah?

77
00:04:32,040 --> 00:04:33,199
What are you doing?

78
00:04:33,439 --> 00:04:36,839
I just petted William.

79
00:04:37,120 --> 00:04:38,199
I'm washing my hands.

80
00:04:38,720 --> 00:04:40,560
I'm about to open a can for him.

81
00:04:40,680 --> 00:04:41,720
Dirty hands

82
00:04:42,079 --> 00:04:43,079
make him throw up.

83
00:04:43,279 --> 00:04:45,399
What a pampered cat.

84
00:04:56,519 --> 00:04:57,720
My rival's rushing me.

85
00:04:57,879 --> 00:04:59,680
He really does think I can't handle it.

86
00:05:00,385 --> 00:05:01,385
What do I do?

87
00:05:01,672 --> 00:05:02,672
Fine.

88
00:05:02,879 --> 00:05:04,678
If he's really that impatient,

89
00:05:05,426 --> 00:05:07,306
I'll go along with it for now.

90
00:05:07,879 --> 00:05:10,439
I'll get him those roles later.

91
00:05:11,319 --> 00:05:13,560
Does it take that long to wash your hands?

92
00:05:14,199 --> 00:05:16,839
Why is it so quiet in there?

93
00:05:17,319 --> 00:05:18,319
Gu Yiliang.

94
00:05:18,721 --> 00:05:19,800
Are you sick?

95
00:05:19,959 --> 00:05:21,136
Don't put off seeing a doctor.

96
00:05:21,160 --> 00:05:22,279
If you're sick, get help.

97
00:05:22,800 --> 00:05:23,800
Gu Yiliang.

98
00:05:23,839 --> 00:05:24,839
Gu Yiliang. Gu...

99
00:05:32,133 --> 00:05:33,113
S-Stop looking.

100
00:05:33,260 --> 00:05:34,660
I was kidding about the challenge.

101
00:05:35,199 --> 00:05:35,800
My knees are jelly.

102
00:05:36,259 --> 00:05:38,019
You win. I'm jelly, okay?

103
00:05:43,319 --> 00:05:44,319
Let's...

104
00:05:46,439 --> 00:05:48,759
L-Let's what?

105
00:05:49,160 --> 00:05:51,439
Get a room? Get it on? Roll camera? Start?

106
00:05:51,759 --> 00:05:52,240
Let's...

107
00:05:52,759 --> 00:05:53,879
Let's...

108
00:05:54,600 --> 00:05:55,600
Let's team up online.

109
00:06:17,120 --> 00:06:18,480
Will you let me go?

110
00:06:19,279 --> 00:06:21,160
I feel awful. I quit.

111
00:06:21,800 --> 00:06:22,800
I quit!

112
00:06:25,720 --> 00:06:26,800
Cheng, you dog.

113
00:06:28,759 --> 00:06:29,959
You're a monster.

114
00:06:30,240 --> 00:06:31,600
I'm already suffering here.

115
00:06:33,160 --> 00:06:34,160
I'm quitting.

116
00:06:34,480 --> 00:06:35,959
A capitalist is trying to kill me!

117
00:06:36,360 --> 00:06:37,879
Quitting isn't an option.

118
00:06:39,120 --> 00:06:40,480
Didn't you read your contract?

119
00:06:41,600 --> 00:06:42,319
Cheng, you dog.

120
00:06:42,600 --> 00:06:43,600
You're a monster.

121
00:06:45,399 --> 00:06:46,639
Feeling better, I see.

122
00:06:46,920 --> 00:06:47,920
Come on.

123
00:06:49,153 --> 00:06:50,600
- Come on.
- Let go of me.

124
00:07:03,680 --> 00:07:04,279
Your fever's gone.

125
00:07:04,399 --> 00:07:05,560
How do you feel now?

126
00:07:06,399 --> 00:07:07,959
Just weak all over.

127
00:07:08,199 --> 00:07:09,319
Nothing else feels wrong.

128
00:07:09,800 --> 00:07:11,279
You had severe heatstroke.

129
00:07:11,399 --> 00:07:13,896
Good thing your friend cooled you down and
got you hydrated in time.

130
00:07:13,920 --> 00:07:15,079
When he brought you in,

131
00:07:15,160 --> 00:07:16,439
you threw up all over him.

132
00:07:16,920 --> 00:07:19,360
He got you cleaned up and on an IV before
he showered.

133
00:07:22,040 --> 00:07:23,079
Get some rest.

134
00:07:23,120 --> 00:07:24,120
Drink plenty of water.

135
00:07:27,720 --> 00:07:29,199
The doctor said to get electrolytes.

136
00:07:41,360 --> 00:07:42,759
Can't you take credit for once?

137
00:07:42,920 --> 00:07:44,240
You make good news sound tragic.

138
00:07:51,240 --> 00:07:52,240
Glad you're okay.

139
00:08:01,920 --> 00:08:03,839
I'm perfectly calm.

140
00:08:03,920 --> 00:08:06,480
I could almost laugh. Yeah, right.

141
00:08:06,505 --> 00:08:08,720
Seriously, how is that fair?

142
00:08:08,879 --> 00:08:12,240
Gu Yiliang, you swept me off my very
straight feet.

143
00:08:12,480 --> 00:08:14,279
Then you slapped me straight again.

144
00:08:14,303 --> 00:08:17,022
Flirting and running should be a crime.

145
00:08:17,785 --> 00:08:20,866
No. I need an explanation.

146
00:08:21,839 --> 00:08:22,439
Have a seat.

147
00:08:22,600 --> 00:08:23,600
Oh.

148
00:08:26,319 --> 00:08:26,800
Huh?

149
00:08:27,160 --> 00:08:28,240
We're not playing Dota?

150
00:08:28,839 --> 00:08:29,839
Let's play League.

151
00:08:30,240 --> 00:08:31,720
I want to play what you like.

152
00:08:32,200 --> 00:08:32,879
Don't worry.

153
00:08:33,039 --> 00:08:34,039
I've played before.

154
00:08:34,720 --> 00:08:36,720
I'm just not very good.

155
00:08:37,240 --> 00:08:38,840
Okay. Dota next time, then.

156
00:08:39,240 --> 00:08:40,240
Mm.

157
00:08:41,639 --> 00:08:43,200
“I want to play what you like.”

158
00:08:43,545 --> 00:08:45,065
Would Guan Yu say that to Zhang Fei?

159
00:08:45,919 --> 00:08:47,760
Is he actually straight?

160
00:08:47,865 --> 00:08:50,465
Did I get the wrong idea earlier?

161
00:08:53,840 --> 00:08:54,840
So...

162
00:08:56,080 --> 00:08:57,080
If...

163
00:08:57,240 --> 00:08:58,960
I mean, hypothetically,

164
00:09:00,360 --> 00:09:02,480
if you had the chance,

165
00:09:03,919 --> 00:09:07,320
and I wanted us to

166
00:09:07,720 --> 00:09:08,960
climb the ranks together

167
00:09:09,639 --> 00:09:11,399
and build a brighter future,

168
00:09:12,919 --> 00:09:14,039
what would you say?

169
00:09:18,480 --> 00:09:19,759
You want to duo in ranked?

170
00:09:21,519 --> 00:09:22,519
Then I'll play Kha'Zix.

171
00:09:23,000 --> 00:09:24,039
I crush it on Kha'Zix.

172
00:09:24,480 --> 00:09:25,840
You trust me that much?

173
00:09:26,120 --> 00:09:27,440
You asked me to play ranked!

174
00:09:28,240 --> 00:09:29,240
So, if...

175
00:09:29,480 --> 00:09:30,519
if I play badly,

176
00:09:31,000 --> 00:09:32,120
you won't yell, right?

177
00:09:34,519 --> 00:09:37,000
Of course not. I'm a chill gamer.

178
00:09:39,679 --> 00:09:40,679
Log in.

179
00:09:41,080 --> 00:09:43,278
Gu Yiliang, get in this teamfight!

180
00:09:43,279 --> 00:09:46,839
What are you doing in the jungle?
Sightseeing? Shopping for souvenirs?

181
00:09:46,840 --> 00:09:48,360
Gu Yiliang!

182
00:09:48,480 --> 00:09:50,600
Could you at least use your passive?

183
00:09:50,679 --> 00:09:54,199
Move that precious
finger and press R. R! R!

184
00:09:54,593 --> 00:09:55,999
Gu Yiliang, saving your ult for next year?

185
00:09:56,000 --> 00:09:58,079
Are your fingers tied in knots?

186
00:09:58,080 --> 00:09:59,959
Forward! Keep going!

187
00:09:59,960 --> 00:10:02,159
Behind you! They're behind you!

188
00:10:02,519 --> 00:10:03,679
Gu Yiliang!

189
00:10:03,840 --> 00:10:06,320
Where are you going? You taking on ten
guys alone?

190
00:10:06,679 --> 00:10:09,159
Get your ass back here!

191
00:10:10,679 --> 00:10:12,440
Gu Yiliang!

192
00:10:18,279 --> 00:10:19,279
A chill gamer?

193
00:10:20,279 --> 00:10:21,600
A full-on warrior Buddha.

194
00:10:24,159 --> 00:10:26,399
I'll get you a fresh one.

195
00:10:27,000 --> 00:10:28,000
Oh.

196
00:10:36,240 --> 00:10:37,240
Was I...

197
00:10:38,240 --> 00:10:39,960
a little too harsh just now?

198
00:10:40,799 --> 00:10:43,080
I just can't figure Gu Yiliang out.

199
00:10:43,759 --> 00:10:46,360
Sometimes he's devious as hell.

200
00:10:46,559 --> 00:10:48,159
Other times he's got one brain cell.

201
00:10:49,639 --> 00:10:50,639
No.

202
00:10:50,879 --> 00:10:51,879
I have to stay strong.

203
00:10:52,200 --> 00:10:53,720
Let him flirt all he wants.

204
00:10:53,840 --> 00:10:55,559
I'll stay straight as steel.

205
00:11:17,559 --> 00:11:18,440
It's late.

206
00:11:18,519 --> 00:11:19,360
No more Coke.

207
00:11:19,440 --> 00:11:20,440
Have some water.

208
00:11:20,559 --> 00:11:21,559
Thanks.

209
00:11:22,240 --> 00:11:22,879
Oh, right.

210
00:11:23,080 --> 00:11:24,200
Where do I sleep tonight?

211
00:11:24,519 --> 00:11:25,519
With me.

212
00:11:33,399 --> 00:11:34,559
Was that something tasty?

213
00:11:36,480 --> 00:11:37,559
Can I have one?

214
00:11:45,559 --> 00:11:47,440
Here's the situation.

215
00:11:47,585 --> 00:11:49,585
Gu Yiliang has three bedrooms.

216
00:11:49,826 --> 00:11:52,585
And yet he asked me to share his.

217
00:11:53,240 --> 00:11:54,320
What does that mean?

218
00:11:54,600 --> 00:11:56,360
A test of your resolve.

219
00:12:00,320 --> 00:12:02,080
If this were fanfic,

220
00:12:02,632 --> 00:12:05,073
he'd walk out of the bathroom any second.

221
00:12:23,320 --> 00:12:24,320
No.

222
00:12:24,600 --> 00:12:25,799
I almost fell for it.

223
00:12:26,320 --> 00:12:27,320
I'll make the first move.

224
00:12:29,600 --> 00:12:30,960
So we're seeing who flirts harder?

225
00:12:31,120 --> 00:12:34,399
I'll make bigger waves than Lake Honghu.

226
00:12:34,519 --> 00:12:38,480
♪ Making waves, wild and free ♪

227
00:12:41,440 --> 00:12:42,440
Where's my phone?

228
00:12:43,240 --> 00:12:44,320
Phone.

229
00:12:52,919 --> 00:12:55,840
The one pose

230
00:12:56,200 --> 00:12:57,679
no straight guy can resist.

231
00:12:58,840 --> 00:12:59,879
The W-sit.

232
00:13:03,279 --> 00:13:04,279
No time.

233
00:13:04,440 --> 00:13:05,440
I choose you,

234
00:13:05,519 --> 00:13:06,519
Pikachu!

235
00:13:17,039 --> 00:13:18,039
Mm.

236
00:13:21,000 --> 00:13:22,000
What's going on?

237
00:13:23,360 --> 00:13:24,840
No, he's about to come out.

238
00:13:40,559 --> 00:13:41,600
What's the problem?

239
00:13:41,960 --> 00:13:43,320
Let's check your blood pressure.

240
00:13:45,399 --> 00:13:47,080
I pulled a muscle in my butt.

241
00:13:47,399 --> 00:13:47,919
What?

242
00:13:47,960 --> 00:13:48,919
His butt hurts.

243
00:13:48,960 --> 00:13:49,600
Oh.

244
00:13:49,919 --> 00:13:51,879
We don't have a proctologist in the ER.

245
00:13:52,559 --> 00:13:53,720
I strained my butt.

246
00:13:54,000 --> 00:13:55,000
Strained it.

247
00:13:57,399 --> 00:13:58,480
The bones look fine.

248
00:13:58,879 --> 00:14:00,440
It's a strained glute.

249
00:14:00,679 --> 00:14:02,480
Did you do anything strenuous recently?

250
00:14:05,759 --> 00:14:07,159
I sat in a W.

251
00:14:10,600 --> 00:14:12,320
I'll prescribe a cream.

252
00:14:12,519 --> 00:14:14,480
Apply it to the sore area three times a
day.

253
00:14:17,559 --> 00:14:18,200
Go pick it up.

254
00:14:18,279 --> 00:14:19,480
Thanks, doctor.

255
00:14:24,000 --> 00:14:25,360
Take it easy, you two.

256
00:14:26,000 --> 00:14:27,080
Couples can experiment,

257
00:14:27,200 --> 00:14:28,759
but go easy on the positions.

258
00:14:29,000 --> 00:14:30,200
Don't push the body's limits.

259
00:14:30,759 --> 00:14:31,159
Okay.

260
00:14:31,200 --> 00:14:32,200
Ah.

261
00:14:33,246 --> 00:14:36,472
So this is what it's like to have the
whole world against you.

262
00:14:36,633 --> 00:14:39,772
Whatever doesn't kill me keeps trying.

263
00:14:54,320 --> 00:14:55,480
Are you laughing at me?

264
00:14:56,240 --> 00:14:57,240
No.

265
00:15:03,240 --> 00:15:03,840
Are you really not?

266
00:15:04,000 --> 00:15:05,000
I'm not.

267
00:15:07,159 --> 00:15:08,480
Good thing it wasn't serious.

268
00:15:08,679 --> 00:15:09,679
Let's go home.

269
00:15:12,399 --> 00:15:14,320
That was so embarrassing.

270
00:15:14,840 --> 00:15:16,519
Am I going to trend tomorrow?

271
00:15:16,840 --> 00:15:17,840
No.

272
00:15:18,080 --> 00:15:19,519
It's a private hospital.

273
00:15:19,720 --> 00:15:20,960
Mr. Cheng recommended it.

274
00:15:21,080 --> 00:15:22,159
They're discreet here.

275
00:15:22,240 --> 00:15:23,840
No one will find out.

276
00:15:24,185 --> 00:15:24,905
Good.

277
00:15:25,139 --> 00:15:26,139
Good.

278
00:15:35,600 --> 00:15:37,240
Mingming has heatstroke?

279
00:15:37,320 --> 00:15:39,159
Why is Mr. Cheng looking after him?

280
00:15:40,113 --> 00:15:42,753
He's not even signed to Hengtu.

281
00:15:43,353 --> 00:15:46,925
What's going on with those two?

282
00:15:50,814 --> 00:15:53,255
Gu Yiliang looks so sweet and restrained.

283
00:15:53,279 --> 00:15:55,639
Behind closed doors, he put the guy in the
hospital.

284
00:15:55,720 --> 00:15:58,120
Wei Yanzi has fight scenes to shoot.

285
00:15:58,320 --> 00:15:59,760
Now he can barely walk.

286
00:16:00,165 --> 00:16:03,360
I guess all sugar daddies are dogs.

287
00:16:06,919 --> 00:16:09,032
I'm pretty sure this hospital has
proctology.

288
00:16:11,840 --> 00:16:12,840
Come outside with me.

289
00:16:15,519 --> 00:16:16,519
Give me a second.

290
00:16:27,919 --> 00:16:29,279
No thanks. I quit.

291
00:16:40,840 --> 00:16:42,039
You and Wei Yanzi.

292
00:16:42,480 --> 00:16:43,600
What's going on?

293
00:16:46,720 --> 00:16:48,200
I chickened out at the last second.

294
00:16:51,006 --> 00:16:52,006
It was my fault.

295
00:16:52,399 --> 00:16:54,080
I wasn't ready.

296
00:16:54,600 --> 00:16:56,840
I wanted to buy a ticket before getting on
the train.

297
00:16:57,840 --> 00:16:58,600
But...

298
00:16:58,639 --> 00:17:00,000
he was in a hurry.

299
00:17:00,879 --> 00:17:02,720
He didn't give me a chance to buy one.

300
00:17:03,639 --> 00:17:05,720
I haven't even gotten him any roles.

301
00:17:07,759 --> 00:17:08,599
He doesn't need them.

302
00:17:08,600 --> 00:17:09,680
That's okay, though.

303
00:17:10,519 --> 00:17:13,079
I've figured out what works for us.

304
00:17:15,079 --> 00:17:16,599
I used to worry

305
00:17:16,759 --> 00:17:18,160
that I was too boring.

306
00:17:19,960 --> 00:17:22,839
So I followed the plot of those novels.

307
00:17:23,119 --> 00:17:24,480
But Wei Yanzi told me

308
00:17:24,559 --> 00:17:26,400
I'm fine the way I am.

309
00:17:27,213 --> 00:17:32,382
So the two of us don't have to
play sugar daddy and kept boy.

310
00:17:33,706 --> 00:17:38,066
I also don't want our relationship
to be purely transactional.

311
00:17:46,400 --> 00:17:47,400
Is that so?

312
00:17:47,880 --> 00:17:48,880
That's good.

313
00:17:51,983 --> 00:17:53,736
Three years earlier.

314
00:17:58,279 --> 00:18:00,200
Come on, let's drink. Cheers!

315
00:18:00,319 --> 00:18:02,279
- Have fun tonight!
- Yan!

316
00:18:03,319 --> 00:18:04,880
I'll have a drink with you.

317
00:18:06,799 --> 00:18:08,079
Want a big brother that bad?

318
00:18:08,319 --> 00:18:09,640
Ask your mom to have one.

319
00:18:10,319 --> 00:18:11,319
Get lost.

320
00:18:11,720 --> 00:18:13,119
He's heartbroken. Let him be.

321
00:18:15,592 --> 00:18:16,592
Oh, come on.

322
00:18:16,680 --> 00:18:18,079
Young Master Cheng.

323
00:18:18,279 --> 00:18:19,279
Look at you.

324
00:18:19,319 --> 00:18:22,200
I brought you out to see all this grass.

325
00:18:22,400 --> 00:18:25,440
See? The grass is green everywhere.

326
00:18:25,839 --> 00:18:29,720
Forget about those little pigs and fish.

327
00:18:30,160 --> 00:18:31,160
You can get lost, too.

328
00:18:33,880 --> 00:18:35,039
If you ask me,

329
00:18:35,160 --> 00:18:36,400
this is partly on you.

330
00:18:36,640 --> 00:18:38,359
Keeping a boy is like fishing.

331
00:18:38,440 --> 00:18:40,400
A little bait just gets them interested.

332
00:18:40,519 --> 00:18:41,160
But you?

333
00:18:41,359 --> 00:18:42,880
You fed him all the good stuff.

334
00:18:43,400 --> 00:18:44,880
Once a fish has had its fill,

335
00:18:44,920 --> 00:18:46,640
of course it swims away.

336
00:18:46,839 --> 00:18:47,839
Right?

337
00:18:51,079 --> 00:18:52,079
You're right.

338
00:18:52,720 --> 00:18:53,920
I was too good to him.

339
00:18:54,720 --> 00:18:56,119
Exactly.

340
00:18:56,200 --> 00:18:57,319
Come on. Drink up.

341
00:18:58,119 --> 00:18:58,960
Well? Go on.

342
00:18:59,119 --> 00:19:00,279
Drink with Mr. Cheng.

343
00:19:09,960 --> 00:19:11,880
Thanks for bringing me that towel earlier.

344
00:19:12,480 --> 00:19:14,359
No problem. We're on the same crew.

345
00:19:14,599 --> 00:19:16,160
We should look out for each other.

346
00:19:24,839 --> 00:19:25,960
Just be careful.

347
00:19:26,079 --> 00:19:27,359
Don't push yourself too hard.

348
00:19:27,720 --> 00:19:29,599
You want to be able to keep doing it.

349
00:19:29,720 --> 00:19:30,839
If it hurts, stop.

350
00:19:30,960 --> 00:19:32,519
They won't feel sorry for you.

351
00:19:35,519 --> 00:19:36,920
So you've “sat” like that, too?

352
00:19:37,599 --> 00:19:39,159
Oh man, it hurts like hell.

353
00:19:39,160 --> 00:19:40,160
Right?

354
00:19:40,759 --> 00:19:43,799
Turns out men's and women's
bodies work differently.

355
00:19:44,640 --> 00:19:46,440
I'm never trying random positions again.

356
00:19:47,240 --> 00:19:49,506
Even a star like Wei Yanzi

357
00:19:49,893 --> 00:19:52,573
has to study positions
to please his sugar daddy.

358
00:19:56,559 --> 00:19:57,880
Mingming, quick question.

359
00:19:58,279 --> 00:19:59,839
What are you and Mr. Cheng?

360
00:19:59,920 --> 00:20:01,278
Did you know him already?

361
00:20:01,279 --> 00:20:02,799
Why'd he bring you to the hospital?

362
00:20:03,680 --> 00:20:05,000
What do you think?

363
00:20:05,599 --> 00:20:06,960
Whatever you and Gu Yiliang are,

364
00:20:07,720 --> 00:20:09,000
that's what we are.

365
00:20:10,079 --> 00:20:11,279
Oh, you too...

366
00:20:11,799 --> 00:20:14,480
Wow, it really is easy to turn gay.

367
00:20:17,640 --> 00:20:18,640
Mingming,

368
00:20:18,680 --> 00:20:19,680
I admire you.

369
00:20:20,440 --> 00:20:22,000
Someone like Mr. Cheng

370
00:20:22,119 --> 00:20:23,759
looks at people like he's saying,

371
00:20:24,000 --> 00:20:25,119
“This isn't personal,

372
00:20:25,240 --> 00:20:27,440
but everyone in this room is trash.”

373
00:20:27,938 --> 00:20:30,538
If you won him over, that's true love.

374
00:20:30,839 --> 00:20:32,359
No. Don't talk nonsense.

375
00:20:32,519 --> 00:20:33,519
Huh?

376
00:20:36,240 --> 00:20:37,240
Take my advice.

377
00:20:37,640 --> 00:20:38,759
For people like us,

378
00:20:38,799 --> 00:20:40,599
you can't afford to catch feelings.

379
00:20:40,640 --> 00:20:41,960
Don't take it seriously.

380
00:20:42,400 --> 00:20:44,400
If you get hurt, you'll have nowhere to
turn.

381
00:20:44,896 --> 00:20:50,255
Heartbreak hurts whether you're straight
or gay, doesn't it?

382
00:20:50,480 --> 00:20:51,480
Oh.

383
00:20:58,960 --> 00:20:59,960
Hey.

384
00:21:00,319 --> 00:21:01,319
Listen to this.

385
00:21:02,279 --> 00:21:03,119
Actually,

386
00:21:03,200 --> 00:21:05,599
Mingming is the boss's husband.

387
00:21:05,640 --> 00:21:06,759
The boss's husband?

388
00:21:06,839 --> 00:21:08,680
Yeah, the boss's husband.

389
00:21:09,599 --> 00:21:10,599
Oh.

390
00:21:11,960 --> 00:21:13,119
Why aren't you surprised?

391
00:21:14,039 --> 00:21:15,160
You already knew?

392
00:21:16,160 --> 00:21:18,240
When I joined Hengtu three years ago,

393
00:21:19,119 --> 00:21:20,920
I heard Mr. Zhu was going to sign with us.

394
00:21:21,279 --> 00:21:24,160
He'd just got a Jinlan nomination for Best
Supporting Actor.

395
00:21:25,359 --> 00:21:27,720
But for some reason, he never signed.

396
00:21:28,960 --> 00:21:31,000
Once I got to know Mr. Cheng,

397
00:21:31,519 --> 00:21:33,759
I found out his family wasn't in showbiz.

398
00:21:33,800 --> 00:21:37,239
He started Hengtu for Mr. Zhu.

399
00:21:37,480 --> 00:21:38,480
Oh.

400
00:21:40,480 --> 00:21:43,000
So Mr. Cheng is the real domineering CEO.

401
00:21:43,200 --> 00:21:45,160
He's pretty bad at being one, though.

402
00:21:45,599 --> 00:21:47,480
Mingming doesn't even have an on-set
assistant.

403
00:21:47,680 --> 00:21:49,080
Heatstroke put him in the hospital.

404
00:21:50,600 --> 00:21:52,560
I don't know exactly what happened.

405
00:21:53,065 --> 00:21:55,305
Only the two of them know the full story.

406
00:21:55,640 --> 00:21:56,880
Good thing he's one of us.

407
00:21:56,960 --> 00:21:58,079
No one else saw.

408
00:22:02,200 --> 00:22:05,160
One look and I knew. A fellow Niangzi
shipper.

409
00:22:05,240 --> 00:22:09,519
What a night. Full of ups and downs downs downs.

410
00:22:16,720 --> 00:22:17,720
Leave it to me.

411
00:22:20,759 --> 00:22:21,799
About what happened...

412
00:22:22,680 --> 00:22:24,160
could you keep it between us?

413
00:22:25,920 --> 00:22:26,920
Any photos?

414
00:22:31,440 --> 00:22:32,920
Could you delete them?

415
00:22:36,359 --> 00:22:38,599
I don't want anyone seeing him like this.

416
00:22:38,799 --> 00:22:41,640
Gu Yiliang, you're making it sound worse.

417
00:22:41,665 --> 00:22:42,979
I'm begging you.

418
00:22:43,003 --> 00:22:44,909
Could you say who you're talking about?

419
00:22:44,933 --> 00:22:48,372
“I don't want anyone seeing ME like this.”

420
00:22:53,480 --> 00:22:54,920
These came out pretty well.

421
00:22:55,000 --> 00:22:56,000
You can keep them.

422
00:22:56,559 --> 00:22:58,200
Just don't spread them around.

423
00:22:58,359 --> 00:22:58,759
Mm.

424
00:22:59,359 --> 00:23:01,680
Could you send me the originals?

425
00:23:09,920 --> 00:23:10,599
Mingming.

426
00:23:10,920 --> 00:23:11,920
What are you doing?

427
00:23:12,279 --> 00:23:14,279
It's so hot. I'm drenched in sweat.

428
00:23:14,559 --> 00:23:15,680
The AC barely works.

429
00:23:15,839 --> 00:23:16,440
I need a shower.

430
00:23:16,440 --> 00:23:17,440
Put this on.

431
00:23:19,079 --> 00:23:20,079
Your fever just broke.

432
00:23:20,359 --> 00:23:21,359
Skip the shower.

433
00:23:30,599 --> 00:23:32,359
How long have you been doing this, kid?

434
00:23:33,960 --> 00:23:34,960
A few years now.

435
00:23:35,759 --> 00:23:36,920
How does it feel, sir?

436
00:23:37,359 --> 00:23:38,359
Mm.

437
00:23:38,480 --> 00:23:40,160
You've improved since a few years ago.

438
00:23:40,400 --> 00:23:41,400
Next time I come in,

439
00:23:41,480 --> 00:23:42,480
I'll ask for you.

440
00:23:50,559 --> 00:23:51,680
Do you remember?

441
00:23:52,039 --> 00:23:53,759
After our first time,

442
00:23:54,480 --> 00:23:55,839
you washed my hair, too.

443
00:23:56,160 --> 00:23:57,160
I was washing your hair,

444
00:23:57,559 --> 00:23:58,599
and you were crying.

445
00:23:59,160 --> 00:24:00,720
I thought you regretted it.

446
00:24:01,599 --> 00:24:03,680
You kept digging your nails into my scalp.

447
00:24:03,720 --> 00:24:04,720
It hurt like hell.

448
00:24:05,200 --> 00:24:06,680
I was scared you'd get mad,

449
00:24:07,000 --> 00:24:08,079
so I just cried.

450
00:24:10,519 --> 00:24:11,519
What about this time?

451
00:24:12,000 --> 00:24:13,000
Why didn't you tell me?

452
00:24:13,880 --> 00:24:14,880
That you ended up in hospital.

453
00:24:19,000 --> 00:24:20,200
I didn't want to bother you.

454
00:24:21,000 --> 00:24:22,680
You'd say I wasn't worth the money.

455
00:24:30,640 --> 00:24:31,720
I won't say that again.

456
00:24:32,680 --> 00:24:35,240
Before, I was afraid the fish would swim away.

457
00:24:38,480 --> 00:24:39,279
All right, all right.

458
00:24:39,359 --> 00:24:40,359
Just finish washing.

459
00:24:41,039 --> 00:24:42,039
It's getting late.

460
00:24:42,240 --> 00:24:43,359
Then go straight back.

461
00:24:45,359 --> 00:24:46,359
Okay.

462
00:25:02,240 --> 00:25:04,480
Life really has its twists and turns.

463
00:25:05,119 --> 00:25:07,000
So cheap.

464
00:25:11,039 --> 00:25:12,039
Sit down for a minute.

465
00:25:16,519 --> 00:25:17,519
I'll be right back.

466
00:25:23,686 --> 00:25:25,060
[Hospital invoice]

467
00:25:25,359 --> 00:25:26,480
I'm so fragile.

468
00:25:27,160 --> 00:25:29,400
This won't mess up tomorrow's big scene,
will it?

469
00:25:51,880 --> 00:25:54,880
You have a room this old-fashioned?

470
00:25:55,559 --> 00:25:58,319
Oh, this was all my grandparents' stuff.

471
00:25:59,920 --> 00:26:02,160
They used to teach at a university.

472
00:26:03,599 --> 00:26:07,359
I grew up with them in faculty housing.

473
00:26:08,519 --> 00:26:11,000
Then, when I was in elementary school,

474
00:26:11,119 --> 00:26:12,119
they both passed away.

475
00:26:21,160 --> 00:26:22,160
Is this...

476
00:26:22,400 --> 00:26:23,880
is this a picture of your mom?

477
00:26:25,799 --> 00:26:26,799
Yeah.

478
00:26:27,319 --> 00:26:28,559
She looks just like you.

479
00:26:28,680 --> 00:26:30,759
The eyes. The nose.

480
00:26:31,799 --> 00:26:33,440
My grandma always said that, too.

481
00:26:34,079 --> 00:26:35,680
And your mom, is she...?

482
00:26:35,759 --> 00:26:36,759
She passed away.

483
00:26:38,240 --> 00:26:39,240
Oh.

484
00:26:41,839 --> 00:26:43,319
When she was pregnant,

485
00:26:44,599 --> 00:26:45,680
she caught Dad cheating.

486
00:26:48,079 --> 00:26:50,200
They divorced after she had me.

487
00:26:51,240 --> 00:26:52,240
Soon after that,

488
00:26:54,519 --> 00:26:55,960
she was diagnosed with cancer.

489
00:26:56,720 --> 00:26:57,720
She didn't have long.

490
00:27:02,799 --> 00:27:06,240
I read somewhere in a magazine

491
00:27:06,400 --> 00:27:10,319
that pregnancy changes your hormone levels

492
00:27:11,720 --> 00:27:14,240
and can trigger certain illnesses.

493
00:27:15,440 --> 00:27:16,200
Do you think...

494
00:27:16,279 --> 00:27:18,319
if she'd found out Dad was cheating

495
00:27:19,480 --> 00:27:20,720
and ended the pregnancy then,

496
00:27:21,799 --> 00:27:23,359
she wouldn't have gotten sick?

497
00:27:24,039 --> 00:27:25,039
Look at her.

498
00:27:25,119 --> 00:27:26,279
She was so young.

499
00:27:29,519 --> 00:27:31,480
I actually asked my mom the same thing.

500
00:27:32,039 --> 00:27:33,039
I asked her,

501
00:27:33,599 --> 00:27:35,039
“Being a single mom is so hard.

502
00:27:35,279 --> 00:27:36,440
If you hadn't had me,

503
00:27:36,880 --> 00:27:38,200
would you have had more options?”

504
00:27:38,839 --> 00:27:40,000
What did she say?

505
00:27:41,079 --> 00:27:42,200
She gave me an earful.

506
00:27:42,519 --> 00:27:43,519
She said,

507
00:27:45,599 --> 00:27:48,079
“Who says a mom can't have better options?

508
00:27:48,319 --> 00:27:50,279
I'll work for what I want.

509
00:27:50,640 --> 00:27:51,960
Sooner or later, I'll get it.”

510
00:27:53,480 --> 00:27:55,039
I think what your mom meant was

511
00:27:55,640 --> 00:27:56,640
she'll get whatever

512
00:27:57,279 --> 00:27:58,279
she sets her heart on.

513
00:27:59,000 --> 00:28:00,119
And everything she has

514
00:28:00,680 --> 00:28:01,839
is something she chose.

515
00:28:02,279 --> 00:28:03,279
Including you.

516
00:28:04,599 --> 00:28:05,599
Then I bet

517
00:28:06,079 --> 00:28:07,519
your mom felt the same way.

518
00:28:08,640 --> 00:28:09,640
Mm.

519
00:28:11,760 --> 00:28:17,193
If I could be as brave as my mom
right now, could I get what I want, too?

520
00:28:18,000 --> 00:28:19,000
Gu Yiliang.

521
00:28:19,240 --> 00:28:20,240
I...

522
00:28:20,880 --> 00:28:21,880
I...

523
00:28:23,039 --> 00:28:24,039
Found it.

524
00:28:26,400 --> 00:28:27,839
You're having trouble walking.

525
00:28:27,920 --> 00:28:29,000
You need this.

526
00:28:38,200 --> 00:28:40,039
Gu. Yi. Liang.

527
00:28:40,612 --> 00:28:43,052
The Monkey King's staff!

528
00:30:29,309 --> 00:30:31,335
Why? Seriously, why?

529
00:30:31,719 --> 00:30:36,492
Whenever I hide in the closet, shipping
us, Gu Yiliang drags me right out.

530
00:30:36,517 --> 00:30:39,278
Then he flirts till I lose my mind,

531
00:30:39,279 --> 00:30:40,559
goes full straight guy again,

532
00:30:40,640 --> 00:30:42,393
and shoves me back in by the hair.

533
00:30:42,417 --> 00:30:44,831
And now he's dead asleep.

534
00:30:45,160 --> 00:30:46,160
Are you asleep?

535
00:30:47,240 --> 00:30:48,920
Oh. No.

536
00:30:49,400 --> 00:30:50,400
What's up?

537
00:30:52,480 --> 00:30:53,759
When I said, “Let's play,”

538
00:30:54,319 --> 00:30:55,799
did that upset you?

539
00:30:56,640 --> 00:30:57,759
No.

540
00:30:59,599 --> 00:31:00,599
Good.

541
00:31:01,079 --> 00:31:03,599
I thought you were so fierce in the game

542
00:31:03,680 --> 00:31:05,400
because you were mad at me.

543
00:31:12,400 --> 00:31:15,519
I'm spent, silent, defeated, hopeless.
Post-nut clarity has set in.

544
00:31:15,599 --> 00:31:18,920
I'm done reading into anything Gu Yiliang
does.

545
00:31:19,000 --> 00:31:21,079
Whatever I think he'll do,

546
00:31:21,160 --> 00:31:24,913
he slips right past
every guess I make.

547
00:31:27,320 --> 00:31:28,519
Wait a second.

548
00:31:28,599 --> 00:31:31,119
What if I think the opposite?

549
00:31:34,599 --> 00:31:38,340
Gu Yiliang definitely won't choke. He
definitely won't choke.

550
00:31:43,279 --> 00:31:47,079
Holy crap. He always does the opposite of
what I predict.

551
00:31:47,160 --> 00:31:49,880
I, Wei Yanzi, am an
expert in all things Gu.

552
00:31:51,200 --> 00:31:53,160
Gu Yiliang is so not gay. Not gay. Not
gay.

553
00:31:53,839 --> 00:31:54,839
I quit smoking.

554
00:31:57,599 --> 00:31:59,960
I used to smoke when I felt down.

555
00:32:01,119 --> 00:32:02,599
I don't think I'll need it anymore.

556
00:32:03,720 --> 00:32:05,712
In a moment like this,
he brings up smoking?

557
00:32:05,913 --> 00:32:07,806
This guy is definitely straight.

558
00:32:08,092 --> 00:32:10,132
Farewell, my ship.

559
00:32:16,599 --> 00:32:20,119
Damn, this reverse-prediction
thing really works.

560
00:32:20,586 --> 00:32:22,000
This has to be witchcraft.

561
00:32:22,079 --> 00:32:25,680
That... doesn't sound very straight.

562
00:32:26,079 --> 00:32:27,680
Because I've got someone now

563
00:32:28,319 --> 00:32:29,680
who always makes me happy.

564
00:32:36,359 --> 00:32:38,799
Welcome back, my sweet ship.
